+# Bun migration
+
+Requires Bun 1.4.4 (the version used for validation). Install with
+`bun install --frozen-lockfile`, then run `bun run typecheck` (or the preserved
+`bun run check` entry point) and `bun run build`.
+
+Preact remains pinned to 10.29.0. Strict checking, automatic Preact JSX, browser
+DOM/ESNext declarations, and the `@lib/` source alias live in tsconfig.json.
+Bun's native checker covers every TypeScript/TSX file under src, including files
+not imported by the main entry point. No TypeScript runtime execution substitutes
+for checking. The unused Deno namespace declarations and Deno configuration have
+been removed.
+
+The build still bundles src/main.tsx for browsers as an IIFE at public/app.js,
+which public/index.html loads as a classic script. Source and HTML asset bytes
+are unchanged. Bun generates different bundle text and size; byte-for-byte
+bundle equivalence is not expected. No new framework or server was added.
+There were no run, serve, test, formatter, or linter tasks in the original project;
+formatter/linter replacement is outside this migration's scope.
+
+Bun tool processes do not reproduce Deno's permission sandbox and run with the
+invoking user's OS permissions. The application remains browser code governed by
+browser security. bunfig.toml disables implicit dotenv loading to preserve the
+original tools' environment handling. Dependency lifecycle scripts were not
+broadly trusted or enabled.
+
+Validation: the original Deno check/build passed. Bun typecheck, check, and build
+passed both in this project and in a clean disposable copy after installation
+from the frozen lockfile, with Deno absent from PATH. A temporary, unimported
+source file with an invalid assignment was rejected by typecheck and then
+removed. Both baseline and Bun bundles produced `Hello Ada` in a DOM-shaped VM
+context and threw `missing app element` when that element was absent. SHA-256
+hashes of public/index.html and public/legal.html match their baseline values.
+There were no existing tests or skips to port. A real browser session, hosted CI,
+and deployment were not exercised; the VM smoke check does not validate all
+browser integration behavior.
